<title>USA: N.Y. business loans fell $53 mln in Jan 29 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans fell $53 mln in Jan 29 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $53 million to $43,266 million in the week ended January 29, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $48 million to $43,498 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $3,062 million to $808,955 million.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
